This directory vendors EasyNLA, a trainer for natural language autoencoders.

Source: github.com/Yooniel/EasyNLA, a fork of Asher Parker-Sartori's EasyNLA
(github.com/asherps/EasyNLA), at commit ef66a76, plus the local modifications
that were used to train the NLAs of the paper's warm-start ablation
(Qwen/Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct, block 20). EasyNLA is itself built on nanoNLA
(github.com/ceselder/nanoNLA). License: MIT, see LICENSE
(Copyright (c) 2026 Asher Parker-Sartori).

Local modifications on top of ef66a76 (all under nla/ unless noted):
  - train_rl_vllm.py: --raw-completion-fallback, --score-truncated,
    --save-raw-evals, --resume-optimizer/--no-resume-optimizer, --failure-mse;
    a step whose DP shard has no scoreable message is skipped on all ranks.
    Without --score-truncated, a truncated held-out completion is now scored as
    an extraction failure (ef66a76 scored it if it parsed).
  - Optional multi-position actor context (sidecar extraction.context_size,
    activation_context column). Datasets without it, including all data of
    the paper, are read as a single position, as in ef66a76.
  - A fixed-norm replacement injection helper (not wired into the trainers).
  - Additional datagen model presets / marker-token cache entries.
  - scripts/init_cold_critic.py (cold-start AR: truncated base + identity
    value head, no task SFT) and scripts/validate_ar_merge.py.
  - Publication edits that do not change behaviour: the default fetch-cache
    directory is derived from tempfile.gettempdir(); a help-text example path;
    tests import the installed package; launchers read paths from the environment.

scripts/regenerate_activations.py is the ef66a76 version, the one that produced
the paper's Qwen2.5 activations (a later local edit added cross-tokenizer
retargeting). configs/datagen/qwen3_8b_finefineweb_100k.yaml is the ef66a76
version with stage0.context_size: 1 made explicit, because the vendored
nla.datagen.run_pipeline defaults to a 3-position actor context that the
paper's data does not use; its output_dir is a relative placeholder.
